00:18:23,440 --> 00:18:28,880
in the VAP store today. There are some AI powered extensions from the community that are also coming in.

165
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:38,240
Now, I mentioned at the beginning that lots of people are justifiably skeptical about AI and we've

166
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:46,080
shared that instinct. One area of concern is around data handling and privacy. What happens to your

167
00:18:46,480 --> 00:18:55,280
highly sensitive data? We designed our approach to AI very much with those concerns in mind. So I'll

168
00:18:55,280 --> 00:19:03,120
explain how we've gone about it. First, you're always in control. All of the features we've added are ones

169
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:10,560
that you need to invoke explicitly. So if you select some text and click explain this, then Burp will use AI.

170
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:16,560
So there's nothing silently processing your data in the background without you asking it to do.

171
00:19:16,560 --> 00:19:25,360
Second, the AI models we use are not being trained on your data. They don't store anything. They don't

172
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:32,640
learn from anything. So if you select some text and click explain this, there is zero risk that your

173
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:39,760
data is ever going to be barfed out by an AI model hallucinating down the line. And it definitely isn't

174
00:19:39,760 --> 00:19:48,080
going to end up in an open S3 bucket where DeepSeq stores all this stuff. Third, when your data is

