00:19:48,080 --> 00:19:54,160
processed by AI, everything goes through our secure infrastructure. We've documented exactly how your

176
00:19:54,160 --> 00:20:01,920
data is handled. This platform is in scope for our bug bounty program. We're confident that everything

177
00:20:01,920 --> 00:20:11,120
is handled securely. Fourth, there's a simple global kill switch in Burp for AI features in the settings.

178
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:21,760
If you don't want to use AI at all, ever in your workflow, then you can just turn off all AI functionality.

179
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:31,200
That will apply both for core Burp features and for BAP store extensions. If you do that, then Burp will

